                        Faustina B.vi, pt. I (ff. 95 and 98--100) were formerly a single
                        MS.</p><p>'Volumen hoc euangelii AEÐELSTAN anglorum basyleos ...
                        dorobernensis cathedre primatui tribuit ecclesie dicate ...' (BL MS Cotton
                        Tiberius A.ii, f. 14v, s. x).</p><p>For the scattered fragments see N.R. Ker
                        in Brit. Mus. Quarterly (1938), pp. 130--1.</p><p>Probably given to
                        Aethelstan by the Emperor Otto (936--973): see Ancient Manuscripts in BM, p.
